# Reverse genetics

**Authors:** Philip Meneely

## Abstract
<p>This chapter focuses on reverse genetics in which the start point is the DNA sequence of a cloned gene, and the mutant phenotype—and hence biological function of the gene—is inferred from that sequence. The chapter starts with an exploration of the reverse genetic analysis carried out on budding yeast and mice. It explores two approaches to reverse genetics: gene disruption and gene replacements. It includes a discussion of the Cre-lox system as an example of gene replacement achieved by site-specific recombination.</p>

**Source:** https://doi.org/10.1093/hesc/9780198809906.003.0009

